From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000019 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Port Bot <port@local>
Date: Sun, 30 Aug 2026 17:17:11 +0200
Subject: 0019: pluggable transports for the pod Terminal tab, merged
 into one dropdown

The pod "Terminal" tab (frontend/public/components/pod-connect.tsx) hardcodes
exec-over-websocket as its only way to reach a container, so a dynamic plugin
cannot offer an alternative (e.g. a VNC framebuffer) for pods that expose one.

Add a small, transport-agnostic extension point: console resolves extensions of
type stei.gr/pod-connect-transport, asks each one to list every connection it
can offer across the whole pod (stei.gr/pod-connect-transport's listConnections,
each already labelled and optionally prioritized by the extension itself), and
merges those into the single "Connecting to" dropdown alongside one plain-exec
Terminal entry per container - transport connections always sort first (by
priority ascending, ties/unset broken by listConnections' own order), then
Terminal entries in pod-manifest order. There is no separate container picker
or "via" dropdown anymore: picking any entry both selects its container and,
for a transport connection, replaces the terminal body with that extension's
component while the exec websocket is not opened at all.

Console core stays free of any VNC/noVNC knowledge; that lives in the
terminal console plugin, which contributes the only such extension today.
When no plugin contributes one, the dropdown is unchanged from before (just
containers, or a bare label when there is only one).

The exec session waits for extension resolution before connecting, so a
container a plugin claims never opens a pod exec that is torn down again a
moment later, and the "exit\r" teardown tolerates a socket that is still
CONNECTING, which switching entries mid-handshake can produce.

A transport can also register toolbar actions (e.g. "send this key
combination to the remote session") via a new onActionsChange callback on
PodConnectTransportProps. When non-empty, they render as a menu in the
toolbar, immediately left of the existing Expand/Collapse control; console
resets them whenever the selected entry changes.
